# The container image build context is the repository root
# (cloudflare-control-plane/wrangler.jsonc sets image_build_context: ".."),
# but the Dockerfile copies only `src/` and the container-runtime package files.
# Everything below is either unused by the image or actively breaks the build.

# macOS AppleDouble sidecars. The repository lives on a filesystem without
# native extended attributes, so macOS writes metadata into `._*` companion
# files. BuildKit's context sender calls xattr() on every entry it walks and
# the driver refuses that call on a sidecar, which failed the whole build with
# `error from sender: failed to xattr .../._.gitignore: operation not permitted`.
**/._*
**/.DS_Store

# Version control, dependencies and build output: not copied by the Dockerfile.
.git
.gitignore
**/node_modules
dist
frontend/dist
.wrangler
**/.wrangler

# Firmware build trees are large and irrelevant to the gateway image.
**/.pio
firmware/**/build

# Local state, logs and scratch data must never enter an image layer.
*.log
coverage
data
*.local
.env
.env.*
